{%- comment -%}
  Authorization policy: admin_only (Layer-2, app-owned; spec §12.2, §5.1).

  Permits the tool only when the resolved PRINCIPAL is an MCP operator. Operators
  are an explicit allowlist in the MCP_ADMIN_USER_IDS constant (comma-separated
  pOS user ids) — no ambient/implicit admin. In on_behalf_of delegation the check
  is against the principal (the human), never the agent (§9.4), so an agent can
  never elevate itself.

  Fail-closed: if the allowlist is unset or the principal is not on it → deny.

  Contract: return { allow, reason }. Receives principal, agent, arguments, tool,
  delegation_mode.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign r = '{}' | parse_json
  assign raw = context.constants.MCP_ADMIN_USER_IDS | default: ''
  assign admins = raw | split: ','
  assign uid = principal.user_id | append: ''
  assign is_admin = false
  for a in admins
    assign a_trimmed = a | strip
    if a_trimmed == uid
      assign is_admin = true
      break
    endif
  endfor
  hash_assign r['allow'] = is_admin
  if is_admin
    hash_assign r['reason'] = 'admin'
  else
    hash_assign r['reason'] = 'not_admin'
  endif
  return r
%}
